Subject: [PATCH 07215/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-34: max_tokens=8192
 fixes round 2 structurally, only with the reminder too

Direct operator follow-up to REQ-33: raise max_tokens to 8192 for the 27B model
and re-run round 2. Targeted single-call replay of the real round-1
counterexample rather than a full fresh episode.

First attempt was a self-caught confound, not a finding: the replay script
forgot to set CARNOT_ARC_REFACTOR_STRUCTURE_REMINDER=1 (REQ-31's fix, read
fresh at call-time). Without it, the model completed naturally within 8192
tokens (proving budget alone was enough room) but invented its own function
name instead of the required engine/is_level_complete -- proving the reminder,
not budget, was what round 2 actually needed. Caught and corrected before
drawing any conclusion.

Corrected, clean, timed re-run (duration_s=195.95, genuine completion
confirmed): with both fixes applied, round 2 succeeds structurally --
proposer_ok=True, natural eos completion, both required functions present.
But the induced code hardcodes literal row/col ranges lifted directly from the
8 shown mismatch examples rather than deriving a general rule -- read as
memorizing the shown failures, not inferring g50t's actual dynamics.
heldout_accuracy was not independently re-measured (would need the real
25-transition corpus); the overfitting read is an informed expectation from
the code's structure, explicitly labelled as such, not presented as measured.

Settles: raising max_tokens to 8192 fixes round 2's structural failure, but
only together with the reminder -- neither alone was sufficient. Does not
settle: whether this closes the accuracy gap -- the hardcoded structure makes
that implausible but unmeasured.

